WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Land measures cut the carbon price from 400 to 180 dollars a ton while protecting food security. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 241. Resistance training during Tier's Epitide treatment, habitats locked inside sea floor nodules, and a science deep dive on mosquito attraction come next. A Potsdam Institute for Climate Impact Research model, covered by Fizz.org, integrated the economy, energy systems, land use, and climate to test pathways that hold warming to war.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.580
1.7 degrees Celsius.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.080
Leaving land unused produced a 3.5% consumption loss

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.540
from 2025 through 2100, while adding every feasible land

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.280
measure brought the carbon price down to $130

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.880
per ton of carbon dioxide, and the consumption loss

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.820
to 1.3%.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:52.900
Biomass land demand range from 66 million hectares to more

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.920
than 300 million hectares depending on the policy mix,

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.120
and that potential is concentrated in the global south,

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:03.160
where food, water, and biodiversity pressures already exist.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.780
A balanced package of residual biomass,

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.440
capped methane and nitrous oxide pricing,

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.820
and global forest conservation held the consumption loss

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.820
to 1.5%.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.740
Lead author Leon Marefort stated that a transformation

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.940
in the land sector allows a slower energy transition

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.760
to reach the same climate target.

00:01:22.741 --> 00:01:25.641
Adults with overweight or obesity taking tears appetite

00:01:25.641 --> 00:01:28.101
were randomized in a nature reported trial

00:01:28.101 --> 00:01:34.901
to resistance exercise or usual activity. 120 participants followed the protocol for 40 weeks,

00:01:35.321 --> 00:01:40.161
with the exercise arm training three times a week. Both groups lost similar total weight

00:01:40.161 --> 00:01:46.721
and fat mass, yet the exercise group lost 1.09 kilograms less total lean soft tissue mass,

00:01:47.201 --> 00:01:50.721
and showed gains rather than losses in upper and lower body strength.

00:01:51.361 --> 00:01:56.721
Adherence to the exercise protocol reached 91%, and the trial found resistance training

00:01:56.721 --> 00:02:01.701
can sit alongside Incretin-based weight loss as a practical adjunct that preserves muscle

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:02.161
function.

00:02:03.182 --> 00:02:08.722
Polymetallic nodules in the Claryon Clipperton Zone were dissected by Marum and As teams

00:02:08.722 --> 00:02:11.702
after collection by box cores and diving robots.

00:02:12.642 --> 00:02:19.962
244 nodules yielded 4,139 individual animals living inside cracks and pores, averaging

00:02:19.962 --> 00:02:23.762
17 per nodule and reaching 245 in one case.

00:02:23.762 --> 00:02:23.862
space.

00:02:24.382 --> 00:02:30.022
Genetic analyses showed the nodule communities were similar across distances up to 1,000 kilometers,

00:02:30.502 --> 00:02:33.422
yet differed markedly from surrounding sediment communities.

00:02:34.082 --> 00:02:39.862
Roundworm abundance inside nodules was about 10% of sediment levels, and copepod abundance

00:02:39.862 --> 00:02:41.582
about 25%.

00:02:41.582 --> 00:02:47.782
The single-celled species Thuramina species 1 was especially common inside nodules, and appears

00:02:47.782 --> 00:02:52.902
adapted to the sheltered spaces, while the nodules themselves grow only a few millimeters

00:02:52.902 --> 00:02:59.502
per million years at depths of 4,000 to 6,000 m. Sabine Galner noted that commercial mining

00:02:59.502 --> 00:03:05.941
may result in irreversible loss of undescribed biodiversity associated with nodules. Most

00:03:05.941 --> 00:03:11.121
people assume every mosquito species keys off the same human scent, so anyone who gets bitten

00:03:11.121 --> 00:03:16.861
often would draw them all in equal measure. In reality, according to Science Daily, each species

00:03:16.861 --> 00:03:22.721
is tuned to its own narrow combination of skin odors, chemicals, and surface bacteria rather than

00:03:22.721 --> 00:03:27.821
a single universal human signal, and that tuning decides which mosquitoes find you on a given

00:03:27.821 --> 00:03:31.561
evening because the blend on your skin matches some species better than others.

00:03:32.281 --> 00:03:37.021
The work documented those distinct profiles across multiple species and showed that the

00:03:37.021 --> 00:03:41.621
differences hold even when the same people are tested again and again, which undercuts

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:45.281
the idea of one type of person who draws every mosquito equally.

00:03:45.921 --> 00:03:50.341
Broad spectrum repellents may therefore miss the specific signals used by the mosquitoes

00:03:50.341 --> 00:03:56.221
that carry particular diseases. Refining repellents around the exact compounds each target species

00:03:56.221 --> 00:04:01.241
detects could improve protection without raising the overall chemical load. And the next step

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:06.161
the team identifies is mapping which bacterial or chemical signals matter most for the species

00:04:06.161 --> 00:04:11.941
that transmit malaria or dengue, so new formulations can be tested against those precise cues.

00:04:12.992 --> 00:04:18.312
Germany's temporary value-added tax reduction from 19% to 16% during COVID

00:04:18.312 --> 00:04:24.072
measured in the review of economic studies, combined survey data, retail purchase records,

00:04:24.432 --> 00:04:29.672
and an economic model to track what households actually spent. Private consumption rose,

00:04:30.032 --> 00:04:34.972
and the largest increases came from lower wealth households, and from younger and middle-aged households.

00:04:35.552 --> 00:04:41.537
Those gains appeared regardless of financial literacy. The first in-depth assessment of coyotes on

00:04:41.537 --> 00:04:47.377
North Carolina barrier islands found population still present despite removal efforts. That ongoing

00:04:47.377 --> 00:04:51.317
presence continues to threaten shore-nesting birds and protected sea turtles.

00:04:52.363 --> 00:04:57.263
Northwestern University researchers tested the Driven App, which pairs weekly self-guided

00:04:57.263 --> 00:05:02.303
mental health exercises with job-seeking tools in a six-week clinical trial aimed at breaking

00:05:02.303 --> 00:05:04.303
the cycle of depression and unemployment.

00:05:05.063 --> 00:05:09.563
Unemployed participants received both the mental health exercises and the job strategies

00:05:09.563 --> 00:05:10.643
in the same program.

00:05:11.643 --> 00:05:16.963
Corey's Shear Waters follow migratory paths that, in a molecular ecology study, tracked

00:05:16.963 --> 00:05:21.463
an individual's genetic ancestry more strongly than conditions in its breeding colony.

00:05:22.343 --> 00:05:26.303
Ancestry predicted the root more reliably than the social environment at the colony.

00:05:27.241 --> 00:05:31.901
University of Liege researchers demonstrated that a herpes virus spreads among European

00:05:31.901 --> 00:05:34.521
eels through biting during aggressive encounters.

00:05:35.141 --> 00:05:40.761
Transmission ran efficiently via those direct bites rather than solely through water, a previously

00:05:40.761 --> 00:05:43.101
unrecognized root for fish virus spread.

00:05:43.101 --> 00:05:50.106
Pet cats and observations of 38 animals reported via science subreddit, meowed four times more

00:05:50.106 --> 00:05:52.786
when owners were present after a problem was introduced.

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:58.066
Vocalization rates ran substantially higher with owners nearby than when the cats were left

00:05:58.066 --> 00:05:59.446
alone with the same problem.

00:06:00.449 --> 00:06:05.489
Artificial intelligence tools show measurable value in some organic chemistry research steps,

00:06:05.809 --> 00:06:11.469
according to a review in chemical society reviews, yet laboratory outcomes diverge from strong

00:06:11.469 --> 00:06:16.469
benchmark scores. Reliability does not always match the benchmark performance the tools

00:06:16.469 --> 00:06:22.219
post on paper, even where they accelerate parts of a workflow. Cornell researchers are

00:06:22.219 --> 00:06:27.399
using existing undersea fiber optic cables to listen for whale vocalizations without deploying

00:06:27.399 --> 00:06:32.819
additional hydrophones. The seafloor infrastructure already in place can monitor those calls for

00:06:32.819 --> 00:06:39.407
conservation. Marine heatwaves that bleach anemones lead clownfish to defend their host more vigorously

00:06:39.407 --> 00:06:42.487
and to behave more aggressively toward other clownfish.

00:06:43.087 --> 00:06:47.407
Home defense and intergroup aggression both rose once the inemones had bleached.

00:06:48.383 --> 00:06:52.963
In brief, a Paul Scherer Institute analysis showed that established hybrid methods for

00:06:52.963 --> 00:06:58.003
quantifying product environmental impacts can be streamlined from four approaches to two

00:06:58.003 --> 00:07:03.763
core ones, supporting more accessible open-source software, and University of Southampton modeling

00:07:03.763 --> 00:07:08.743
found that redirecting shipping lanes to protect whale sharks carries very little additional

00:07:08.743 --> 00:07:15.143
fuel cost. Before we go, mapping which bacterial or chemical signals matter most for malaria and

00:07:15.143 --> 00:07:20.843
dengue mosquitoes is the next step named in the attraction work, so new formulations can be tested

00:07:20.843 --> 00:07:26.143
against those cues. That covers today's science and health news. Share this with someone who's

00:07:26.143 --> 00:07:32.203
curious about the latest research. I'm Patrick in Vancouver. See you next time. If this show earns a

